.TH LOGSTORE\-WRITER 1 "2026-11-10" "unheaded 6ce98954" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
logstore\-writer \- Insert the journal rows Vector posts into the Well's log_events table, capped (S\-E1\-LIVE Evening 16).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B logstore\-writer
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Insert the journal rows Vector posts into the Well's log_events table, capped (S\-E1\-LIVE Evening 16).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-addr \fISTRING\fR
listen address (default :19140)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-bytes \fIN\fR
ceiling on what log_events may hold, in bytes; over it /ingest answers 503 (default 4294967296)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-rows\-per\-minute \fIN\fR
rows accepted in one clock minute; past it /ingest answers 429 (default 6000)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH NOTES
The Well login comes from WELL_HOST, WELL_USER, WELL_PASSWORD, WELL_DB, WELL_SSLMODE, WELL_SSLROOTCERT; the ingest token from LOGSTORE_INGEST_TOKEN.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
logstore\-writer \-\-max\-rows\-per\-minute 6000 \-\-max\-bytes 4294967296
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
